@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFBFD
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #52677D
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
title Agemem · project memory architecture

actor "Coding agent\nCodex / Cursor / Claude Code" as Agent
component "MCP server\nFive explicit memory tools" as MCP #DFEAF6
component "Memory engine\nScopes · filters · budgets · citations" as Engine #DFEAF6
package "Project checkout" {
  folder "memory/*.md\nReadable working state" as Bank #E4F1E8
  database ".agemem/local/notes.sqlite\nScreened durable notes" as Notes #E4F1E8
  database ".agemem/local/sources.sqlite\nOriginal evidence + vectors" as Sources #E4F1E8
  file ".agemem/config.json\nProject settings" as ProjectConfig
}
file "Private config.yaml\nSchema version · provider · credentials" as UserConfig
component "Typed decision adapter\nJev / QSIV / ollaya / cascade" as Decisions #FFF0D7
cloud "Hosted Jev" as Jev #FFF0D7
component "Local GPU QSIV\nIsolated Python runtime" as QSIV #FFF0D7
component "Source retrieval\nBM25 / hybrid / adapted RAW-RAG" as Retrieval #DFEAF6

Agent --> MCP : recall / capture / remember\nindex / maintain
MCP --> Engine
Engine --> Bank : read current context
Engine --> Notes : write / select / consolidate
Engine --> Sources : archive / snapshot
Engine --> Retrieval : retrieve original evidence
Retrieval --> Sources
Engine --> Decisions : screen and select memories
Decisions --> Jev : hosted choice
Decisions --> QSIV : local choice
UserConfig ..> Engine : global defaults
ProjectConfig ..> Engine : project overrides
note bottom of Agent
  The coding agent writes the final answer.
  Capture and bank updates are explicit.
end note
note bottom of Decisions
  Decision models do not write the final answer.
  Cascade can deliberately fall back to hosted Jev.
end note
@enduml
